= The Murder of Erzberger

On 26 August Matthias Erzberger of the Centre, who signed the armistice in the forest of Compiègne and was hounded by the nationalist press ever since, is shot dead while out walking at Bad Griesbach in the Black Forest. The two killers, Heinrich Tillessen and Heinrich Schulz, are former naval officers of the Organisation Consul, the secret society that grew out of the Ehrhardt Brigade. They escape to Hungary.

Part of the nationalist press says openly that Erzberger had it coming. The President issues an emergency decree for the protection of the Republic. In Munich, Kahr's government refuses to apply it. On 31 August hundreds of thousands march in the cities of the Reich against the murderers.

- @march: March with the SPD, the USPD and the unions.
- @defence: Form workers' defence squads.
- @demand: Demand that the Republic disarm its enemies.

